---
name: is_user_allowed
redirect_to: '{% if context.current_user %}/verify-2fa{% else %}/sign-in{% endif %}'
metadata: {
    "auth_policy_name": "User Permission"
}
---

{% liquid
  graphql check_2fa_setup = 'account/check_2fa_setup'
  assign current_user = check_2fa_setup.current_user
  assign user = current_user.client | first

  comment
    User must exist. If the profile is missing, deny rather than redirecting by
    default to prevent accidental access on partially-created accounts.

    When several policies on a page fail, the platform uses the redirect of the
    policy that was created first, not the first one listed in the page. So this
    redirect does not rely on is_user_logged_in winning: a signed-out visitor is
    sent to /sign-in from here too, and only a signed-in user who still has to
    pass 2FA goes to /verify-2fa.
  endcomment
  if user == blank
    echo false
    return
  endif

  comment
    2FA is passed per session, not per user: the 2FA page stores the user id in
    this session only after a valid code. Another browser signed in with the
    password alone has no such value and is sent to verify-2fa.
  endcomment
  assign current_user_id = current_user.id | append: ''
  assign passed_user_id = context.session.two_factor_user_id | append: ''

  if user.otp_configured == true and passed_user_id != current_user_id
    echo false
  else
    echo true
  endif
%}
